               <exData contentType="text/html">
                  <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/"><p style="font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:0in">INSTRUCTIONS:<span style="xfa-spacerun:yes"> </span><span style="font-weight:normal">When you filed your Free Application for Federal Student Aid (FAFSA), the FAFSA processor sent you a response indicating their records showed that a previous loan is in default, discharged, or that you have filed bankruptcy. Based on that response, the federal government requires that we obtain information from you to confirm your continued eligibility to receive federal funds.</span><span style="font-weight:normal;font-style:italic"> Incomplete documents will not be returned.</span><span style="font-weight:normal"><span style="xfa-spacerun:yes"> </span></span><span style="font-weight:normal;font-style:italic">They will be disposed of in a secure manner, per university policy.</span><span style="font-weight:normal"><span style="xfa-spacerun:yes"> </span></span><span style="font-weight:normal;font-style:italic">This will delay processing.<span style="xfa-spacerun:yes"> </span></span></p><p style="font-style:italic;letter-spacing:0in"><br/></p><p style="letter-spacing:0in">Your loan history from the National Student Loan Data System (<a href="http://www.nslds.ed.gov/">www.nsldsfap.ed.gov</a>) may show that your loans are defaulted. You may call the U.S. Department of Education at 1.800.621.3115 for assistance or for information regarding your loan.</p><p style="letter-spacing:0in"><br/></p><p style="letter-spacing:0in">We cannot proceed with the review of your financial aid eligibility until you submit a copy of the requested documentation that is appropriate to you situation and it is verified as resolved.</p></body>
               </exData>
            </value>
            <font typeface="Arial"/>
            <margin topInset="0.5mm" bottomInset="0.5mm" leftInset="0.5mm" rightInset="0.5mm"/>
